      "track": "section-b",
      "markdown": "The NAND(not-and) function has many applications. The truth table of NAND, with two inputs, is as follows\n\n| A | B | A NAND B |\n|---|---|---|\n| T | T | F |\n| T | F | T |\n| F | T | T |\n| F | F | T |\n\nLet's use Q to represent the NAND function. Therefore the NAND of X and Y is (XQY), and this result is also a boolean expression. Also A and B themselves are boolean expressions. For example, the NOT function of A can be expressed as (AQA).\n\nPlease note that brackets in the above example are compulsory, no mark will be given for answers that miss brackets in the following questions."
    },
